


The istream_readline function "istream_readline.h"

            The istream_readline function attempts to read a
            non-blank line from stdin. On success, the
            corresponding string is found in the array
            specified by #0. The new-line character is
            discarded; the The istream_readline function
            terminates the program on file error,
            end-of-file, if the array is filled before a
            new-line character is encountered, or if too
            many blank lines are read (KIS).
